# ============================================================================
# target.param  --  ArduPilot Copter parameters for the TARGET / practice quad
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Board / firmware target : KakuteH7   (Holybro Kakute H7 V1.5, the ORDERED FC)
#   Flash the ArduCopter build for board name "KakuteH7"  --  NOT "KakuteH7v2"
#   and NOT the -bdshot / -Wing variants.  This is the V1 board.
#   src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/common-holybro-kakuteh7.html
#
# ⛔ FIRMWARE VERSION IS PINNED: ArduCopter 4.7.0.
#   Verified 2026-07-26: firmware.ardupilot.org/Copter/stable/KakuteH7/
#   firmware-version.txt reads "4.7.0-FIRMWARE_VERSION_TYPE_OFFICIAL".
#   PARAM NAMES MOVED, so this is not decoration. Between 4.5 and 4.7 ArduPilot
#   renamed four of the params this file sets, and Mission Planner SKIPS an
#   unknown name with a warning rather than failing -- a silently dropped write
#   that is invisible in the write direction:
#       GPS_TYPE      -> GPS1_TYPE      (4.6: AP_GPS::Params subgroup prefix "1_")
#       WPNAV_SPEED   -> WP_SPD         (Copter 4.7 GOBJECTPTR(wp_nav, "WP_"),
#                                        and the UNIT changed cm/s -> m/s)
#       WPNAV_ACCEL   -> WP_ACC         (same rename; cm/s/s -> m/s/s)
#       ANGLE_MAX     -> ATC_ANGLE_MAX  (AC_AttitudeControl, "ATC_" prefix;
#                                        centidegrees -> DEGREES, range 10..80)
#       ARMING_CHECK  -> ARMING_SKIPCHK (AP_Arming "SKIPCHK"; INVERTED sense --
#                                        it is the bitmask of checks to SKIP)
#   Sources (read at tag Copter-4.7.0): libraries/AP_GPS/AP_GPS.cpp
#   AP_SUBGROUPINFO(params[0], "1_"), libraries/AC_WPNav/AC_WPNav.cpp
#   AP_GROUPINFO("SPD"/"ACC") + AC_WPNav.h WP_SPD_DEFAULT 10.0f,
#   libraries/AC_AttitudeControl/AC_AttitudeControl.cpp AP_GROUPINFO("ANGLE_MAX"),
#   libraries/AP_Arming/AP_Arming.cpp AP_GROUPINFO("SKIPCHK", ... , 0),
#   ArduCopter/Parameters.cpp GOBJECT/GOBJECTPTR prefixes.
#   DO NOT load this file on 4.5.x or 4.6.x without re-checking those five names.
#   ON BUILD DAY: after loading, READ THE PARAMS BACK off the FC and diff against
#   this file. A dropped write is only visible in the read direction.
#   src (bom): docs/project_state.json bom_tiers[0] ("ArduPilot target KakuteH7
#              -- flash THAT not v2"); docs/hardware_order_list.md (E)
#
# Airframe (ORDERED 2026-07-20, bom_tiers Tier-1):
#   TBS Source One V6 5" frame | EMAX ECOII 2207 1900KV x4 | Tekko32 F4 Metal
#   65A 4-in-1 ESC (DShot) | Matek M10Q-5883 GPS+compass | RadioMaster RP1 V2
#   ELRS nano RX wired CRSF | RadioMaster Pocket M2 ELRS TX (bind as MODEL 1) |
#   CNHL 6S 1500 mAh LiPo.
#
# ROLE: MOVER ONLY. This quad flies a scripted AUTO box/line for the tripod
#   field test (docs/tripod_test_protocol.md). It is NOT the interceptor.
#   This file sets the target-specific WIRING + LOGGING + AUTO SPEED + FAILSAFES
#   + flight-mode/kill switch mapping. It deliberately does NOT contain a flight
#   TUNE -- maiden as a plain quad, then run AUTOTUNE (see README.md). PID gains,
#   filter, and notch params are left at the KakuteH7 firmware defaults.
#
# FORMAT: Mission Planner "Full Parameter List -> Load" file.
#   * Lines beginning with "#" are comments.
#   * Every data line is exactly   PARAM_NAME,VALUE
#   * Each param is preceded by a one-line WHY + doc source.
#   * "(firmware default, stated)" marks a value equal to the KakuteH7 hwdef or
#     the Copter default, written explicitly so build day is copy-paste, not
#     guesswork. All OTHER lines are non-default and are cited.
#
# AFTER LOADING: reboot the FC (BATT_MONITOR, BRD_ALT_CONFIG, and serial protocol
#   changes only take effect after a reboot), then do accel + compass cal and the
#   RC/motor-order/kill-switch verification in README.md before the first arm.
# ============================================================================


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FRAME
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Quad. Sets FRAME_CLASS so the 4 motor outputs get MotorN functions.
# src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/frame-type-configuration.html
FRAME_CLASS,1
# X layout (TBS Source One V6 is an X frame). Verify actual motor ORDER and
# spin DIRECTION in Mission Planner Motor Test before flight (Betaflight numbering
# differs from ArduPilot). src: frame-type-configuration.html
FRAME_TYPE,1


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BOARD ROTATION  --  the flight controller is mounted BACKWARDS (2026-11-14)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Builder found it on the bench: the Kakute's arrow points at the tail, the
# same mistake as the interceptor's Pixhawk (SENS_BOARD_ROT=4 there). 4 =
# Yaw180. Rotates the gyro, accelerometer and any on-board compass into the
# airframe's axes; needs a reboot. The external GPS compass has its own
# setting (COMPASS_ORIENT, found automatically by the compass calibration).
# Observed on the bench: resting roll/pitch read -3.4 / -4.3 deg before the
# write and +3.4 / +4.3 after the reboot, which is what a 180 degree turn
# must do.
# CALIBRATE THE ACCELEROMETER AND COMPASS *AFTER* THIS IS SET.
# This does NOT move the motors: the motor order below was verified corner by
# corner on 2026-10-13, and the record does not say which end was called
# "front" that day. RE-RUN THE MOTOR TEST, PROPS OFF, before the first arm:
# motor A must be the FRONT-RIGHT of the real nose. If A is back-left, the
# order was set against the board's arrow and SERVO1..4_FUNCTION need the
# 180 degree swap (33<->34, 35<->36) or the first take-off flips.
# src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/common-sensor-offset-compensation.html
# src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html (AHRS_ORIENTATION)
AHRS_ORIENTATION,4


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MOTORS / ESC  --  Tekko32 F4 Metal 65A 4-in-1, DShot
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DShot600. The Tekko32 is a digital BLHeli32 ESC -> DShot needs no ESC
# calibration and has no PWM pulse jitter. MOT_PWM_TYPE 4..7 = DShot150..1200.
# src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/common-dshot-escs.html
MOT_PWM_TYPE,6
# Auto-enable BLHeli passthrough + ESC telemetry on every DShot output so the
# Tekko32 can be configured from Mission Planner (Setup > Optional HW > BLHeli).
# src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/common-dshot-escs.html
SERVO_BLH_AUTO,1
# 6S thrust-vs-voltage scaling upper bound (4.20 V x 6 = 25.2 V). Keeps hover
# thrust consistent across the pack. src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.html
MOT_BAT_VOLT_MAX,25.2
# 6S scaling lower bound (3.30 V x 6 = 19.8 V). src: motor-thrust-scaling.html
MOT_BAT_VOLT_MIN,19.8


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FIRST-FLIGHT SETUP FOR A 5-INCH QUAD  (added 2026-11-14, before the maiden)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT a tune: the rate PIDs stay at firmware defaults. These are the settings
# ArduPilot says to make BEFORE the first flight, which the firmware ships
# sized for a 10-inch quad (read off this board 2026-11-14: gyro filter 20 Hz,
# thrust expo 0.65). Same lesson as the interceptor's ADR-0134: defaults sized
# for a big slow airframe.
# Values = Mission Planner's "Initial Parameter Setup" helper for prop 5 in,
# 6S LiPo (4.2 / 3.3 V per cell), formulas read from its source
# (MissionPlanner GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigInitialParams.cs, fetched
# 2026-11-14) and recomputed here. ArduPilot's own table for 5-inch props says
# gyro filter 80 Hz and expo 0.55; the helper's curve gives 75 and 0.49.
# src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/setting-up-for-tuning.html
# IF IT OSCILLATES ON THE FIRST HOP: land at once and halve ATC_RAT_RLL_P/I/D
# and ATC_RAT_PIT_P/I/D (the documented response).
# src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/initial-tuning-flight.html
#
# Gyro low-pass, Hz: max(20, round(289.22 * prop^-0.838)) = 75.
INS_GYRO_FILTER,75
# Accelerometer low-pass, Hz (helper constant; firmware default is 20).
INS_ACCEL_FILTER,10
# Rate-loop target and D-term filters = gyro filter / 2.
ATC_RAT_RLL_FLTT,37.5
ATC_RAT_RLL_FLTD,37.5
ATC_RAT_PIT_FLTT,37.5
ATC_RAT_PIT_FLTD,37.5
ATC_RAT_YAW_FLTT,37.5
# Yaw error filter, Hz (helper constant; firmware default 2.5).
ATC_RAT_YAW_FLTE,2
# Max commanded angular acceleration, DEG/s/s on 4.7 (the helper divides its
# centidegree figures by 100 when the 4.7 names ATC_ACC_* exist, as they do
# on this board). Roll/pitch: -2.613267 p^3 + 343.39216 p^2 - 15083.7121 p +
# 235771 = 168,610 -> 1686. Yaw: -900 p + 36000 = 31,500 -> 315.
ATC_ACC_R_MAX,1686
ATC_ACC_P_MAX,1686
ATC_ACC_Y_MAX,315
# Thrust curve: min(round(0.15686 ln(prop) + 0.23693, 2), 0.80) = 0.49.
MOT_THST_EXPO,0.49
# Starting guess for hover throttle, deliberately LOW; the firmware learns the
# real value in flight (MOT_HOVER_LEARN=2 on this board). A 2207 1900KV on 6S
# hovers a light 5-inch far below the 0.35 default.
MOT_THST_HOVER,0.2
# Stabilize throttle mix for a first flight (already the firmware default; set
# to 0.5 after the first good flight, per the helper's closing note).
ATC_THR_MIX_MAN,0.1


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BATTERY MONITOR  --  onboard voltage + 4-in-1 ESC current sense
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Analog Voltage AND Current. KakuteH7 has an onboard voltage divider (B+) and
# reads the Tekko32's current signal on the "Cur" pad. Default is 0 (disabled),
# so this MUST be set. Takes effect after a reboot.
# src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/common-holybro-kakuteh7.html (Battery Monitor)
BATT_MONITOR,4
# Voltage ADC pin -- KakuteH7 hwdef HAL_BATT_VOLT_PIN. (firmware default, stated)
BATT_VOLT_PIN,10
# Current ADC pin -- KakuteH7 hwdef HAL_BATT_CURR_PIN. (firmware default, stated)
BATT_CURR_PIN,11
# Voltage divider multiplier -- KakuteH7 hwdef HAL_BATT_VOLT_SCALE 11.0.
# Sanity-check reported pack voltage against a cell checker; nudge if it reads off.
# src: common-holybro-kakuteh7.html
BATT_VOLT_MULT,11.0
# Amps-per-volt for the current sensor -- KakuteH7 hwdef default 59.5. The ACTUAL
# scale depends on the Tekko32 shunt, so CALIBRATE it: fly/hover a known load,
# compare logged Ah drawn to the charger's replaced mAh, scale this value.
# src: common-holybro-kakuteh7.html ; https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/common-power-module-configuration-in-mission-planner.html
BATT_AMP_PERVLT,59.5


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BATTERY FAILSAFE  (6S)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Low-battery threshold 3.60 V/cell (21.6 V) sustained >10 s -> low action.
# src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/failsafe-battery.html
BATT_LOW_VOLT,21.6
# Critical threshold 3.30 V/cell (19.8 V) -> critical action.
# src: failsafe-battery.html
BATT_CRT_VOLT,19.8
# Low action = RTL (mover flies home rather than dropping). 0:None 1:Land 2:RTL.
# src: failsafe-battery.html
BATT_FS_LOW_ACT,2
# Critical action = Land immediately (can't make it home). 1:Land.
# src: failsafe-battery.html
BATT_FS_CRT_ACT,1


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RC LINK  --  RadioMaster RP1 V2 ELRS receiver on CRSF (SERIAL6 / UART6)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Kakute H7 R6 pad is a TIMER-based RC input by default (good for SBUS/PPM,
# one-way only). ELRS CRSF is a full-duplex UART protocol (RC + link-stats
# telemetry), so R6/T6 must be remapped to USART6. BRD_ALT_CONFIG=1 does exactly
# that on this board. Takes effect after a reboot.
# src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/common-holybro-kakuteh7.html (RC Input / CRSF note)
BRD_ALT_CONFIG,1
# RCIN protocol on SERIAL6 (= UART6, the remapped R6/T6). CRSF is auto-detected
# among the serial RC protocols; baud is set automatically by the firmware.
# src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/common-tbs-rc.html ; common-holybro-kakuteh7.html
SERIAL6_PROTOCOL,23
# No inversion / half-duplex -- ELRS CRSF is plain full-duplex UART. (default, stated)
# src: common-holybro-kakuteh7.html
SERIAL6_OPTIONS,0
# RSSI / link-quality taken from the receiver protocol (CRSF LinkStatistics).
# 3 = "Receiver Protocol". src: https://www.expresslrs.org/quick-start/ardupilot-setup/
# ; https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/common-rssi-received-signal-strength-indication.html
RSSI_TYPE,3


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GPS + COMPASS  --  Matek M10Q-5883 on SERIAL3 (UART3)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GPS protocol on UART3. (firmware default, stated -- KakuteH7 GPS pad is UART3.)
# src: common-holybro-kakuteh7.html
SERIAL3_PROTOCOL,5
# Auto-detect the u-blox M10 receiver. (firmware default, stated)
# RENAMED in Copter 4.6: GPS_TYPE -> GPS1_TYPE (AP_GPS::Params subgroup prefix
# "1_", AP_GPS.cpp). On 4.7 the OLD name does not exist, and Mission Planner
# skips an unknown name rather than erroring -- benign here only because the new
# param already defaults to 1. src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/common-gps-for-position.html
GPS1_TYPE,1


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AUTO LEG SPEED  --  tripod matrix needs >=9 m/s passes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 10 m/s horizontal AUTO speed. The protocol's full-speed passes push toward
# >=9 m/s (docs/tripod_test_protocol.md 4.4); 10 clears that with margin.
# This equals the firmware default but is set explicitly to make the >=9 m/s
# requirement unmistakable on build day. A per-leg DO_CHANGE_SPEED in the mission
# (gen_tripod_mission.py) can still slow individual "control" passes.
# RENAMED + RE-UNITED in Copter 4.7: WPNAV_SPEED (cm/s) -> WP_SPD in METRES/s.
# The old line said 1000; on 4.7 that name does not exist, and the number would
# have been 100x wrong if the rename had been done without the unit.
# src (read at tag Copter-4.7.0): AC_WPNav.cpp AP_GROUPINFO("SPD", ...,
# _wp_speed_ms, WP_SPD_DEFAULT), @Units m/s @Range 0.10 20.00; AC_WPNav.h
# `#define WP_SPD_DEFAULT 10.0f`; Parameters.cpp GOBJECTPTR(wp_nav, "WP_").
WP_SPD,10
# Horizontal AUTO acceleration (m/s/s). The firmware default 2.5 is sluggish ->
# a short ~30 m leg may never reach 9-10 m/s. 3.5 lets the target hit speed on
# the leg. Verify actual leg speed in the log on the maiden AUTO run.
# RENAMED + RE-UNITED in 4.7: WPNAV_ACCEL (cm/s/s, was 350) -> WP_ACC (m/s/s).
# src: AC_WPNav.cpp AP_GROUPINFO("ACC", ..., _wp_accel_mss,
# WPNAV_ACCELERATION_MS), @Units m/s/s @Range 0.50 5.00 (default 2.5).
WP_ACC,3.5
# Max lean angle, 35 deg. The default 30 deg can cap top speed; 35 gives the lean
# headroom to hold 9-10 m/s.
# RENAMED + RE-UNITED in 4.7: ANGLE_MAX (centidegrees, was 3500) ->
# ATC_ANGLE_MAX in DEGREES. 3500 would now be rejected outright: the firmware
# range is 10..80. src: AC_AttitudeControl.cpp AP_GROUPINFO("ANGLE_MAX", ...,
# _angle_max_deg), @Units deg @Range 10.0 80.0; Parameters.cpp
# GOBJECTVARPTR(attitude_control, "ATC_").
ATC_ANGLE_MAX,35


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATAFLASH LOGGING  --  field_score.py needs POS + GPS on the onboard microSD
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copter default log set (176126): logs GPS, ATTITUDE, IMU, CTUN/NTUN, MOTBATT,
# and the POS vehicle-position estimate. scripts/field_score.py reads the .BIN's
# POS message (preferred) and falls back to GPS -- both are present in this set.
# Written to the Kakute's microSD (see README.md -- NO card = NO scored pass).
# src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/common-logs.html (LOG_BITMASK, default 176126)
LOG_BITMASK,176126
# Do not log on the bench while disarmed -- log from arm. (firmware default, stated)
# src: common-logs.html
LOG_DISARMED,0
# Rotate to a fresh .BIN on each disarm -> one file per flight/pass, which is
# exactly what field_score.py + the session log (protocol 11) want.
# src: common-logs.html (LOG_FILE_DSRMROT)
LOG_FILE_DSRMROT,1


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FLIGHT MODES + RC KILL  (RadioMaster Pocket M2)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mode switch on RC channel 6 (builder call 2026-10-25, matching the Pocket as
# bound: 3-pos switch -> CH6, 2-pos kill -> CH5). History: the 2026-10-04 B1
# finding moved modes OFF channel 5 because ELRS HARD-LIMITS AUX1 to 2
# positions regardless of TX switch config; with only THREE modes flown, any
# AUX2+ channel carries a 3-pos fine (ELRS hybrid mode: AUX2-7 are 3-pos;
# wide mode: 64-pos), so ch6 works and ch12 (ELRS's suggested default) is not
# required. Modes must still NEVER live on ch5.
# src: https://www.expresslrs.org/software/switch-config/ (AUX1 "is always a
# 2-position channel"; hybrid/wide aux resolution).
FLTMODE_CH,6
# Mode-switch map (builder call 2026-11-14, replacing Loiter / RTL / Auto). He
# named the positions from the switch as it sat on the bench; it read 2011 (UP)
# at that moment, so:
#   switch UP     = Loiter (5)   GPS position hold, ArduPilot's equivalent of
#                                PX4 Position. Same thumb position as Position
#                                on the interceptor.
#   switch MIDDLE = AltHold (2)  holds height, pilot flies level; no GPS
#                                needed. Same position as Altitude on the
#                                interceptor.
#   switch DOWN   = Auto (3)     flies the mission loaded from QGroundControl.
#                                (The interceptor has Stabilized here.)
# Auto sits at an END of the travel, so going Loiter <-> AltHold never passes
# through it, and one click up from Auto is AltHold. ArduPilot will not ARM
# in Auto with this parameter set (AUTO_OPTIONS=0; mode_auto.cpp
# allows_arming at Copter-4.7.0), so the mission can only be started in the air.
# There is NO Stabilize position. ArduPilot's first-flight page says to fly
# first in Stabilize and not to take off in AltHold until the height
# controller has been tested: the builder's call, flagged to him 2026-11-14.
# MEASURED on the board 2026-11-14: the switch reads 987 down and 2011 up, and
# its centre is 1499 -- 9 microseconds above the edge between mode bands 3 and
# 4 (bands change at 1231 / 1361 / 1491 / 1621 / 1750, RC_Channel.cpp at
# Copter-4.7.0). So bands 3, 4 and 5 ALL carry the middle mode: a centre that
# drifts either way still reads AltHold. lint_param.py enforces it.
# src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/flight-modes.html
FLTMODE1,3
FLTMODE2,3
FLTMODE3,2
FLTMODE4,2
FLTMODE5,2
FLTMODE6,5
# RC channel 5 (ELRS AUX1, the 2-pos switch) = ARM / DISARM (builder call
# 2026-11-14: "the position it's in now should be unarmed"; it read 999, DOWN).
#   switch DOWN = disarmed.  switch UP = arm (all arming checks still run).
# This switch is ALSO the target's RC kill: moving it DOWN in flight disarms at
# once and the motors stop. Read at Copter-4.7.0: RC_Channel.cpp
# do_aux_function_armdisarm (LOW -> disarm(AUXSWITCH)) and
# AP_Arming_Copter.cpp disarm(), which refuses an in-flight disarm only for
# ground-station and stick-gesture requests, not for a switch. It is NOT
# recoverable the way Motor Emergency Stop (31, used here until today) or the
# interceptor's kill switch are: a bumped switch at height is a dropped
# aircraft. A power-up with the switch UP does not arm (init_aux_function
# skips ARMDISARM). Stick arming (throttle down + yaw right) still works too.
# ELRS sends AUX1 in every packet -- the lowest-latency channel on the link.
# src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/common-auxiliary-functions.html (153)
RC5_OPTION,153
# ch6 is the MODE channel, so it must carry NO aux function: a stale
# RC6_OPTION=31 here would fire Motor Emergency Stop on the Auto detent
# (switch high) -- a guaranteed mid-air kill. Pinned 0 and
# lint-enforced.
RC6_OPTION,0


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ARMING
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ALL pre-arm checks ON. Left ON per the build spec -- do NOT disable checks to
# "get it flying"; fix the flagged cause instead.
# RENAMED + INVERTED in Copter 4.7: ARMING_CHECK (a bitmask of checks to RUN,
# was 1) -> ARMING_SKIPCHK, the bitmask of checks to SKIP. 0 = skip nothing =
# every check on. Writing 1 here would now SKIP a check instead of enabling one.
# src (read at tag Copter-4.7.0): AP_Arming.cpp
# AP_GROUPINFO("SKIPCHK", 13, AP_Arming, checks_to_skip, 0);
# Parameters.cpp GOBJECT(arming, "ARMING_", AP_Arming_Copter).
# src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/prearm_safety_check.html
ARMING_SKIPCHK,0


# ============================================================================
# FAILSAFE / GEOFENCE  --  RC loss = come home (decided 2026-11-14)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The target now has its OWN transmitter, and its mission LOOPS FOREVER
# (DO_JUMP, gen_loop_mission.py). "Continue the mission on RC loss" (the old
# OPTION A, FS_OPTIONS bit0, written for one shared transmitter and a mission
# that ended by itself) would now mean a target with no radio link flying laps
# until the battery failsafe. So RC loss returns it to the arming point in
# every mode, Auto included. The geofence stays as the second bound.
# src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/radio-failsafe.html
# ============================================================================
# RC failsafe armed: 1 = Enabled, always RTL. src: radio-failsafe.html
FS_THR_ENABLE,1
# 0 = no exceptions: RC loss in Auto ALSO returns home (bit0 would continue the
# mission). lint_param.py refuses bit0 set. src: radio-failsafe.html (FS_OPTIONS)
FS_OPTIONS,0
# Geofence ON. src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.html
FENCE_ENABLE,1
# Fence type = Altitude + Circle + Polygon (bitmask 1+2+4). src: common-ac2_simple_geofence.html
FENCE_TYPE,7
# 80 m circular fence around home. **TUNE to your actual field.** metres.
# CENTRED ON *HOME* = THE POINT WHERE YOU ARM. A mission whose far waypoint is
# more than (FENCE_RADIUS - margin) from the arming point breaches mid-leg and
# FENCE_ACTION=1 brings the target home. The mission generators print the
# arm-within budget for the route they emitted.
# src: common-ac2_simple_geofence.html (FENCE_RADIUS)
FENCE_RADIUS,80
# 50 m altitude ceiling. **TUNE to your field / airspace authorization.** metres.
# src: common-ac2_simple_geofence.html (FENCE_ALT_MAX)
FENCE_ALT_MAX,50
# Breach action = RTL or Land (fires even mid-AUTO if the target leaves the box).
# 0:Report 1:RTL/Land 2:Land 3:SmartRTL 4:Brake. src: common-ac2_simple_geofence.html (FENCE_ACTION)
FENCE_ACTION,1
# GCS failsafe disabled -- the target has no companion/telemetry link on it.
# (firmware default, stated) src: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/gcs-failsafe.html
FS_GCS_ENABLE,0
# ============================================================================
# End target.param

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# MOTOR MAPPING + DIRECTION -- RE-MEASURED AT THE BENCH 2026-10-13 (FC #2).
# Board #1's 2026-09-23 mapping (S3=34, S4=35, RVMASK=6) died with that
# board: the replacement FC's ESC harness is a hand-built pigtail soldered
# to the Tekko32's gold pads (the original 8-pin socket is flaky under
# flex), and its wire order swaps the two left-side channels and flips
# both left motors. Fixed in software, verified motor-by-motor (A-D hit
# the right corner, right direction) after a reboot, builder-confirmed.
# THESE VALUES ARE BUILD-SPECIFIC: a re-solder or new ESC re-earns them.
SERVO1_FUNCTION,36
SERVO2_FUNCTION,33
SERVO3_FUNCTION,35
SERVO4_FUNCTION,34
# DShot reversal mask for FC #2's pigtail wiring (bits SERVO2|SERVO4 = 2|8 = 10).
SERVO_BLH_RVMASK,10
# Without this ArduPilot never SENDS DShot commands, so RVMASK is silently
# inert -- found live 2026-09-23 (mask persisted, motor still spun CW).
SERVO_DSHOT_ESC,1
